  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="11.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:ICn">I Cn</ref> 11.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="11.2" corresp="#wit-g-a">⁊ gá ælc cyricsceat into þam ealdan mynstre be ælcon frigan heorðe.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="11.2" corresp="#wit-a">⁊ ga ælc cyricsceat into þam ealdan mynstre be ælcan frigean heorðe.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="11.2" corresp="#wit-q">Et eat omnis cyricsceat ad matrem ęcclesiam per omnes liberas domos.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="11.2" corresp="#wit-g-a">⁊ gá ælc cyricsceat into þam ealdan mynstre be ælcon frigan heorðe.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a">And ga ælc cyricsceat into þam ealdan mynstre be ælcon frigan heorðe.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-g-a">And all the church dues from every free household shall go to the old parish church.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a">And all Church dues from every free household are to go to the old minster.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Und jede Kirchensteuer von jedem freien Herde gehe in die alte Pfarrkirche.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And let every church-scot from every free hearth go to the old minster.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares II Eg 2.2.</note>
        <note type="translator" source="#rabin-doml">old minster: That is, the principal church in a region to which the smaller (and newer) parish churches are subordinate.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
